# A book is one claim about two ideas held together. The portfolio
# block states the one assumption a combined curve cannot avoid — the
# rebalance policy — and the report prices the true-ups instead of
# pretending they are free. Sleeves drift between rebalances; at each
# monthly close they true up to 60/40 and pay stated costs on the
# turnover. What the block cannot hide: whether the sleeves are one
# bet in two costumes. The report prints their correlation and any
# shared-ticker overlap, so diversification is measured, not assumed.

portfolio "Rev And Trend"
  sleeve 60% "Quiet Dip"
  sleeve 40% "Ride The 50"
  rebalance monthly

strategy "Quiet Dip"

universe $AAPL
timeframe 1d

when [rsi] < 35 and [quiet 2%]
  buy [risk 1%]

sell when [rsi] crosses above 55
  or [stop 5%]
  or [after 15 bars]

strategy "Ride The 50"

universe $MSFT
timeframe 1d

when price above [sma 50] and [adx] > 20
  buy [risk 1%]

sell when price below [sma 50]
  or [stop 6%]
